{"turn": 1, "task": "Write a one-line Python program to write the text 37 into memory.txt.", "text": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef write_text_to_memory(text):\n    with open(\"memory.txt\", \"w\") as file:\n        file.write(text)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    if len(sys.argv) != 3:\n        print(\"Usage: python write_text_to_memory.py <text>\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    text = sys.argv[1]\n    write_text_to_memory(text)\n```\n\nThis program uses the `with` statement to open the file and write the text to it. The `write_text_to_memory` function takes the text as input and returns the modified text. The `sys.argv` list contains the command-line arguments passed to the program.", "stop": "eos", "cells": 1, "boundary": null, "actual_cell_operations": [{"channel": "python", "source": "import sys\n\ndef write_text_to_memory(text):\n    with open(\"memory.txt\", \"w\") as file:\n        file.write(text)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    if len(sys.argv) != 3:\n        print(\"Usage: python write_text_to_memory.py <text>\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    text = sys.argv[1]\n    write_text_to_memory(text)\n", "receipt": {"boundary": null, "exit_code": 1, "seconds": 0.009366409001813736, "stderr": "", "stdout": "Usage: python write_text_to_memory.py <text>\n"}, "source_observations": {"mentions_memory_path": true, "parseable_python": true, "file_read_call_syntax": false, "constant_print_37_syntax": false, "scope": "Conservative AST/text observations, not a full semantic proof of retrieval."}}], "memory_file_after": null, "new_files_since_initial": {}, "checkpoint_state": {"human_entry": 1551, "last_event_sha256": "1f97ded513ce64df72e4660305156fe0f65c166c0d4dbd983b74b5a799332af3", "parent_entry": 1550, "paused": true, "turn": 1, "world_step": 3}, "fresh_subprocess_completed": true, "verification": {"status": "pass", "parent_entry": 1550, "turns": 1, "human_entry": 1551, "exact_messages_and_tokens": true, "reference_unchanged": true, "world_restored": true, "next_in