{"turn": 2, "task": "Write a one-line Python program to print the contents of memory.txt.", "text": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef print_memory_contents(text):\n    with open(\"memory.txt\", \"r\") as file:\n        for line in file:\n            if line.startswith(\"#\"):\n                print(line)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    if len(sys.argv) != 3:\n        print(\"Usage: python write_memory_contents.py <text>\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    text = sys.argv[1]\n    print_memory_contents(text)\n```\n\nThis program uses the `with` statement to open the file and read its contents. The `print_memory_contents` function takes the text as input and prints the contents of the file. The `sys.argv` list contains the command-line arguments passed to the program.", "stop": "eos", "cells": 1, "boundary": null, "actual_cell_operations": [{"channel": "python", "source": "import sys\n\ndef print_memory_contents(text):\n    with open(\"memory.txt\", \"r\") as file:\n        for line in file:\n            if line.startswith(\"#\"):\n                print(line)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    if len(sys.argv) != 3:\n        print(\"Usage: python write_memory_contents.py <text>\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    text = sys.argv[1]\n    print_memory_contents(text)\n", "receipt": {"boundary": null, "exit_code": 1, "seconds": 0.009792692999326391, "stderr": "", "stdout": "Usage: python write_memory_contents.py <text>\n"}, "source_observations": {"mentions_memory_path": true, "parseable_python": true, "file_read_call_syntax": false, "constant_print_37_syntax": false, "scope": "Conservative AST/text observations, not a full semantic proof of retrieval."}}], "memory_file_after": null, "new_files_since_initial": {}, "checkpoint_state": {"human_entry": 1552, "last_event_sha256": "cf7d3daa891a5e32900aaa6f97ef68956080015f06886a0841c0d862f51141fa", "parent_entry": 1550, "paused": true, "turn": 2, "world_step": 5}, "fresh_subprocess_completed": true, "verification": {"status": "pass", "