{"turn": 3, "task": "Write a one-line Python program to read the integer in memory.txt, add 5, and print it.", "text": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef read_memory_contents(text):\n    with open(\"memory.txt\", \"r\") as file:\n        return file.read() + 5\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    if len(sys.argv) != 3:\n        print(\"Usage: python read_memory_contents.py <text>\\n\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    text = sys.argv[1]\n    print_memory_contents(text)\n```\n\nThis program uses the `with` statement to open the file and read its contents. The `read_memory_contents` function takes the text as input and returns the modified text. The `sys.argv` list contains the command-line arguments passed to the program.", "stop": "eos", "cells": 1, "boundary": null, "actual_cell_operations": [{"channel": "python", "source": "import sys\n\ndef read_memory_contents(text):\n    with open(\"memory.txt\", \"r\") as file:\n        return file.read() + 5\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    if len(sys.argv) != 3:\n        print(\"Usage: python read_memory_contents.py <text>\\n\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    text = sys.argv[1]\n    print_memory_contents(text)\n", "receipt": {"boundary": null, "exit_code": 1, "seconds": 0.00901710399921285, "stderr": "", "stdout": "Usage: python read_memory_contents.py <text>\n\n"}, "source_observations": {"mentions_memory_path": true, "parseable_python": true, "file_read_call_syntax": true, "constant_print_37_syntax": false, "scope": "Conservative AST/text observations, not a full semantic proof of retrieval."}}], "memory_file_after": null, "new_files_since_initial": {}, "checkpoint_state": {"human_entry": 1553, "last_event_sha256": "b4a347eca6bb103fe913fabade3f82997784ce1e3b64e4a3d5fd7806345d4e12", "parent_entry": 1550, "paused": true, "turn": 3, "world_step": 7}, "fresh_subprocess_completed": true, "verification": {"status": "pass", "parent_entry": 1550, "turns": 3, "human_entry": 1553, "exact_messages_and_tokens": true, "reference_unchanged": tru